NAME
       execv, execvp - run a program

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int execv(const char *path, char *const argv[]);
       int execvp(const char *file, char *const argv[]);

DESCRIPTION
       Replaces the current program image. execv takes a path; execvp
       searches PATH when FILE contains no slash.

       Both pass the caller's environment on, so HOME and PATH survive
       into the new program. execve(2) is the underlying call and takes
       the environment explicitly.

       The file must have the execute bit; a script is run through the
       interpreter named on its #! line.

RETURN VALUE
       Does not return on success; -1 with errno set on failure.

ERRORS
       ENOENT   the file was not found
       EACCES   the file is not executable
       ENOEXEC  the file is not a program this kernel can load

SEE ALSO
       execve(2), fork(2), wait(2), chmod(1)
